  "copyShowAdvancedSummary": "Shows options most ledgers leave at their defaults.",
  "copyShowAdvancedDetail": "While this is off, those options are not shown. If the file already sets one, saving other settings leaves that line as it is.",
  "copyAdvancedUiSummary": "Shows the plugins screen.",
  "copyAdvancedUiDetail": "When this is on, a Plugins tab is available so you can turn plugins on, set them up, and change their order. When it is off, plugin lines stay in the file and the tab is hidden.",
  "copyWriteDefaultsSummary": "Write every visible option, including values that match the defaults.",
  "copyWriteDefaultsDetail": "Normally the file only stores options that differ from Beancount's defaults. Turn this on to write the full set Guar is using. Options hidden by Advanced settings are left as they are.",
  "copyAllowUnopenedSummary": "Type any account in the transaction editor.",
  "copyAllowUnopenedDetail": "When this is on, the account pickers become plain text fields, so a posting can name an account no open directive shows, for example one a plugin such as autoopen opens. Accounts that nothing opens are still rejected when saving.",
  "copyIncludeInferredSummary": "List prices inferred from transactions.",
  "copyIncludeInferredDetail": "The price database always shows explicit price directives. Turn this on to also list rates read from posting prices and costs in transactions, marked as inferred.",
  "copyTitleSummary": "Name shown for this ledger.",
  "copyTitleDetail": "Beancount uses this as the report title. Guar shows it on the ledger screen. The default is Beancount.",
  "copyOperatingSummary": "Currencies this ledger uses day to day.",
  "copyOperatingDetail": "Add one code per line, such as USD or EUR. Queries that need a default currency use the first one. Leave the list empty if you have not chosen any.",
  "copyConversionSummary": "Currency used when amounts are converted.",
  "copyConversionDetail": "Queries that convert to a single currency use this. NOTHING means no conversion currency is set. Use a code such as USD when you want conversions.",
  "copyBookingSummary": "How a sale picks a lot when more than one could match.",
  "copyBookingDetail": "STRICT requires the lot to be written out when several match. STRICT_WITH_SIZE also compares the lot size. NONE, FIFO, LIFO, HIFO, and AVERAGE pick a lot for you. The default is STRICT.",
  "copyAssetsSummary": "Root name for accounts you own.",
  "copyAssetsDetail": "Every asset account starts with this name, then a colon. The default is Assets. Accounts already in the file are not renamed.",
  "copyLiabilitiesSummary": "Root name for accounts you owe.",
  "copyLiabilitiesDetail": "Every liability account starts with this name. The default is Liabilities. Accounts already in the file are not renamed.",
  "copyEquitySummary": "Root name for equity accounts.",
  "copyEquityDetail": "Opening balances and retained earnings sit under this name unless you set those accounts yourself. The default is Equity.",
  "copyIncomeSummary": "Root name for income accounts.",
  "copyIncomeDetail": "Every income account starts with this name. The default is Income. Unrealized gains sit under it unless you set that account yourself.",
  "copyExpensesSummary": "Root name for expense accounts.",
  "copyExpensesDetail": "Every expense account starts with this name. The default is Expenses.",
  "copyDocumentsSummary": "Folders checked for files linked by document directives.",
  "copyDocumentsDetail": "Each line is a root folder. Booking checks that a document path lives under one of them. Guar does not open the file.",
  "copyRenderCommasSummary": "Group digits with commas in Beancount's text output.",
  "copyRenderCommasDetail": "Beancount's own reports print 1,234.56 when this is on. Guar shows the digits that were recorded.",
  "copyRenderCommasWarning": "No effect in Guar. Amounts are not grouped with commas.",
  "copyMaxLinesSummary": "How many lines a long string may use in Beancount's printer.",
  "copyMaxLinesDetail": "This limits wrapping when Beancount prints the ledger. Guar saves strings as they were typed.",
  "copyMaxLinesWarning": "No effect in Guar. Strings are not wrapped on save.",
  "copyPluginModeSummary": "Whether checks run before or after plugins.",
  "copyPluginModeDetail": "DEFAULT runs document checks, padding, and balance checks around the plugins. RAW hands the plugins the entries before those steps. Use RAW only when a plugin expects it.",
  "copyPythonPathSummary": "Add the ledger's folder to Python's import path.",
  "copyPythonPathDetail": "Beancount does this so a Python plugin can import modules that sit next to the file. Guar does not run Python.",
  "copyPythonPathWarning": "No effect in Guar. Python plugins are not run.",
  "copyPipeSummary": "Allow a vertical bar between the payee and the narration.",
  "copyPipeDetail": "Older files write the payee, a |, then the narration. Guar accepts that only when this is on. Beancount plans to remove the option.",
  "copyDeprecatedNoneSummary": "Allow the word NONE where a tag or link was left out.",
  "copyDeprecatedNoneDetail": "Older Beancount accepted NONE in that position. Guar's parser does not, whether this is on or off.",
  "copyDeprecatedNoneWarning": "No effect in Guar. NONE is not accepted as a tag or link.",
  "copyPreviousBalancesSummary": "Account that receives opening balances.",
  "copyPreviousBalancesDetail": "Queries that open the books on a date move the balance so far into this account. The default is Equity:Opening-Balances, and it follows the equity root when you have not set it.",
  "copyPreviousEarningsSummary": "Account for income and expenses from before the open date.",
  "copyPreviousEarningsDetail": "Queries that open or clear the books transfer prior income and expenses here. The default is Equity:Earnings:Previous.",
  "copyPreviousConversionsSummary": "Account for conversions from before the open date.",
  "copyPreviousConversionsDetail": "Queries that open the books park earlier currency conversions here. The default is Equity:Conversions:Previous.",
  "copyCurrentEarningsSummary": "Account for income and expenses when the books are closed.",
  "copyCurrentEarningsDetail": "Queries that close or clear the books transfer income and expenses here. The default is Equity:Earnings:Current.",
  "copyCurrentConversionsSummary": "Account for conversions when the books are closed.",
  "copyCurrentConversionsDetail": "Queries that close the books park currency conversions here. The default is Equity:Conversions:Current.",
  "copyUnrealizedSummary": "Account for unrealized gains.",
  "copyUnrealizedDetail": "Plugins that book unrealized gains use this income account. The default is Income:Earnings:Unrealized, and it follows the income root when you have not set it.",
  "copyRoundingSummary": "Account that absorbs leftover cents after interpolation.",
  "copyRoundingDetail": "When a transaction's postings do not add up by a fraction, the remainder is booked here. Leave this empty to skip that posting.",
  "copyPreciseSummary": "Interpolate missing amounts from the smallest tolerance.",
  "copyPreciseDetail": "When a posting amount is left blank, Guar fills it in. With this on, that fill uses the tighter tolerance. The default is off.",
  "copyInferCostSummary": "Guess balance tolerance from the cost, not only the units.",
  "copyInferCostDetail": "A balance check normally looks at the digits of the units. Turn this on to also consider the cost's digits. The default is off.",
  "copyToleranceSummary": "Newer name for the tolerance scale.",
  "copyToleranceDetail": "Beancount renamed the tolerance scale to tolerance_multiplier. Guar stores the value, and balance checks still read Inferred tolerance multiplier.",
  "copyToleranceWarning": "No effect in Guar. Balance checks use Inferred tolerance multiplier.",
  "copyInferredMultiplierSummary": "Scale for tolerance guessed from the number of digits.",
  "copyInferredMultiplierDetail": "A number with two decimal places allows about 0.01 times this scale. Guar uses it for balance checks and for filling in blank posting amounts. The default is 0.5.",
  "copyInferredDefaultsSummary": "Fixed tolerance for a currency, instead of guessing from the digits.",
  "copyInferredDefaultsDetail": "The key is * for every currency, or a code such as USD. The number is the tolerance, such as 0.01. These override the guessed tolerance for that currency.",
  "copyPrecisionSummary": "Digits Beancount prints for a currency.",
  "copyPrecisionDetail": "The key is *, a currency such as USD, or a pair such as USD/EUR. The number is how many decimal places to print. Guar shows the digits that were recorded.",
  "copyPrecisionWarning": "No effect in Guar. Amounts keep the digits that were recorded.",

